Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 22:42:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] SSE liveness counter

Adds GET /global/live-sessions returning the set of session IDs with
at least one open SSE subscription on /event?sessionID=<id>. Used by
hivemind to filter list_sessions to sessions someone is actively
attached to.

Mechanism:
  - event.ts: module-level Map<string, number> keyed by sessionID.
    Increment when /event opens with the query param; decrement in the
    abort handler. Subscriptions without the param keep working
    unchanged but don't contribute to liveness.
  - global.ts: new GET /global/live-sessions route returns
    { sessions: liveSessions() }, which is just the keys with count > 0.

Pairs with the TUI patch that adds ?sessionID=<current> to its event
subscription; the TUI is the only built-in client today, so we get
accurate liveness as soon as both ship. The server-side patch is
forwards-compatible with unmodified clients (their streams just don't
register).
